db/ref 17592186382020} :answer-field/id #uuid "26f6dddc-207b-5ada-a853-8f975e7c1162" :answer-field/key "field-9" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382018} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93229c20-24ce-5d7e-bcb8-de40cff8311c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382024} {:answer/id #uuid "dc1a7775-fa89-5a70-99d7-50a32a2340da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382025} {:answer/id #uuid "df827696-cccc-524f-8dd7-9a486d655d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382026} {:answer/id #uuid "57eef191-29b6-557c-bb0d-c552c0ee5cd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382027} :answer-field/id #uuid "82392c3a-f0f6-5951-a926-f66c0787e9b1" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382023}] :question/id #uuid "8d1f0a35-56cb-5370-99fa-b599f7ccb0a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-363840" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$  select the correct options in the computations of the matrix $U$ below.From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce the singular values ${\\sigma }_{1}=5$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\n\nNow, we compute the $1$st column of $U.$ It is given by:\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${u}_{1}=\\,\\,$ |  | $\\frac{3}{5}$ |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal.\n\nHence, we must find vectors $u=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}]^{T}$ such that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to \n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nChoosing ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ as free variables, the general solution is given by:\n\n|  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} |  |  |\n|  |  | ${x}_{3}$ |  |  |\n\nthat we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the two linearly independent solutions are already mutually orthogonal, we only need to normalize them. Hence, we obtain the second and third columns of $U:$\n\n| | ${u}_{2}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-7}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $0$ |  |  |  | | | ${u}_{3}=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-8}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-9}} |  |  |  | |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${u}_{2}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-7}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $0$ |  |  |  |\n| ${u}_{3}=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ |  |  |\n|  | {{field-8}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-9}} |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=5$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\nAlso, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$\n\nTherefore, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find vectors \n\n$$\nu=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nsuch that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0$ and $‖u‖=1.$\n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{5}{x}_{1}+\\frac{3}{5}{x}_{2}=0\\,⟹\\,4{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get the general solution \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{2}{{\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{x}_{3}{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables.\n\nNotice that the two linearly independent solutions ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ are mutually orthogonal. Therefore, we only need to normalize them. This gives the second and third columns of $U:$   \n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,{u}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix $U$ could be the following:\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} & -\\frac{3}{5} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1624144f-dc91-5236-84ee-18b96e8277af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407934} {:answer/id #uuid "1f0a89b3-42e1-5c0c-9f1d-976b0b80e3f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407939} {:answer/id #uuid "746511ed-c96a-5c0b-a954-73fab4f89071" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407934} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ef2a40d-dd8f-5054-9101-9b4095ee0f14" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e47d3ea-4750-55d7-9ad9-f144dbee61aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407943} {:answer/id #uuid "9c719bc8-cc87-56ef-930a-6bf23b501c80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407975} {:answer/id #uuid "cea590ba-fbf3-55d0-a265-d70d43b6166d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407988} {:answer/id #uuid "de95b675-12ca-5166-875b-1b757ac71752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407975} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c9d1bfc-8364-5715-9bb8-cb03bdb6692f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408005} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "643472bb-dd98-50e4-aff0-bc71a00a2ebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407958} {:answer/id #uuid "7bff4c82-4456-5898-b454-3fd5aee86c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407967} {:answer/id #uuid "945556be-8f84-5bd3-b5af-929f33248c9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407973} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d270f4-9dfe-58