ref 17592186525752} {:answer/id #uuid "e3af9b95-6ba3-5980-9529-8aa1c1a85764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525534} :answer-field/id #uuid "da09beb8-b5fd-5f20-9435-ebf709c0ccbd" :answer-field/key "field-9" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525955} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9eb5f05f-1f6a-507e-8738-2f2123b40919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525610} {:answer/id #uuid "aa3bd616-b6aa-5ef0-80f3-fdf67937b79e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525637} {:answer/id #uuid "cce7551b-697b-543d-a753-797afb60888e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525715} {:answer/id #uuid "d6c554c6-a35a-5d6d-8c85-3d1083908bcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525715} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfb56aec-cbc6-5eb1-b7e3-d0d0324dfd8c" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525958} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "425b853c-d1b5-583d-a5ce-9de98a7e2c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525373} {:answer/id #uuid "57a041f1-60e0-5295-b25b-a25100f70274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525432} {:answer/id #uuid "9f361199-bd83-56dd-94a9-78c6195e7a40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525432} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2cafab0-8360-5672-9122-b5764a0bc21c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525972}] :question/id #uuid "03ae1482-39ea-5fad-a59a-df13068a2393" :question/math-academy-id "q-363219" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{30} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$  select the correct options in the computations of the matrix $U$ below.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce the singular values ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{30}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\n\nNow, we compute the $1$st column of $U.$ It is given by:\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${u}_{1}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  |  | $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}$ |  |  |\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal.\n\nHence, we must find vectors $u=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}]^{T}$ such that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nChoosing ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ as free variables, the general solution is given by:\n\n|  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} |  |  |\n|  |  | ${x}_{3}$ |  |  |\n\nthat we can rewrite as:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nNext, we orthogonalize ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ using the Gram-Schmidt process to get the corresponding orthogonal vectors ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nLet ${c}_{1}={b}_{1},$ then:\n\n|  |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${c}_{2}=\\frac{2}{5}\\,\\,$ |  | $1$ |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-7}} |  |  |\n\nFinally, normalizing orthogonal vectors ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ we obtain the second and third columns of $U:$   \n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\">\n                ${u}_{2}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"90px\">\n                {{field-8}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-9}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\">\n                ${u}_{3}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"90px\">\n                {{field-10}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-11}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{30}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\nAlso, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$\n\nTherefore, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}}[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find vectors \n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nsuch that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0$ and $‖u‖=1.$\n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}{x}_{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}{x}_{2}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,-2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get the general solution \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables. \n\nNotice that the two linearly independent solutions ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ are *not* mutually orthogonal. Therefore, we have to orthogonalize them using the Gram-Schmidt process. So, let \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}={b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{2} & ={b}_{2}-\\frac{{b}_{2}\\cdot {c}_{1}}{{c}_{1}\\cdot {c}_{1}}{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{(-1)}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{2}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, normalizing orthogonal vectors ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ we obtain the second and third columns of $U:$   \n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{u}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix $U$ could be the following:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{30}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & 0 & \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{30}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35b4ca0a-9edf-58bb-9973-6bce1087bbbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545309} {:answer/id #uuid "a59b3207-17fe-54db-93f1-48d5b2c6af0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545503} {:answer/id #uuid "ea49e934-713f-59c1-9cd8-b71c13888df8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545503} :answer-field/id #uuid "15df1cd3-e39e-5404-bf3f-832cf64e6231" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2256e52a-32fe-533f-a968-350b0804bcd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545271} {:answer/id #uuid "73227208-2ac3-5483-acf4-40615f09bc37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545415} {:answer/id #uuid "86672d15-cbce-5422-b86e-38403f8dfa29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545453} {:answer/id #uuid "ea9e97ff-c4d6-58a7-b13d-49fdf4bcff6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545635} :answer-field/id #uuid "558c9eb5-ede5-54a6-bb1f-e7b9797a4197" :answer-field/key "field-10" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545709} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43810ef2-8d84-5de3-8727-a74ca97da0c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545326} {:answer/id #uuid "459dc813-deb7-58ab-9dd6-7676ac00ff86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545332} {:answer/id #uuid "66cca1ae-ab4f-5d9b-9fc5-ee65dd6ea081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545396} {:answer/id #uuid "ec18891d-99bd-56c3-879d-8763adf3113b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/i