-3)-1(10-9) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4-3-1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, none of the statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9c8a655-dc30-5747-b5e0-efd4fa464943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437794} {:answer/id #uuid "b3238a25-1600-54c9-a92e-d6b1f31166ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437794} :answer-field/id #uuid "0457a549-1799-5124-a11e-6cbe8bf02f40" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438926} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86770289-d595-5a74-8241-7f7eaf943501" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437796} {:answer/id #uuid "0065df67-0fde-5ae4-ab1b-04075255afaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437797} :answer-field/id #uuid "48c446f0-c232-5d1a-a9fa-08c4d973bbe4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438927} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d221ff-7342-5189-8083-2e45e2305d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437798} {:answer/id #uuid "db168e14-a68a-5486-95d1-8d4686854e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437799} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5f6d45-4846-5d6c-b409-f20f073263eb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438928}] :question/id #uuid "898815e0-65a8-55f9-b81f-a64efbb5e7e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-128476" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $T$ is a singular matrix\n- **II.** $T$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- **III.** $det(T)=-30$\n\n \n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1-3)-3(2-1)-5(6-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-3-25 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=-30\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96a78a3a-a96f-5296-bb6f-17bd0c2c1029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437812} {:answer/id #uuid "8a41bcde-2807-5a96-8245-df7493039a41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437813} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d87a851-8d26-5425-83e8-dba94be07b21" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438935} {:answer-fie